FP6 stage-2 adbd hardening, on top of the mobile-nixos adbd patches
(ubports android-tools-pkg 128a2506 + 0001..0006).

* RSA key authorization is always on (there is no ro.adb.secure property
  on NixOS). Keys: /etc/adbd/adb_keys (declarative) and
  /var/lib/adbd/adb_keys (approved on the phone).
* adbd drops to the account in $ADBD_USER (must be non-root) before it
  touches USB: setgid/initgroups/setuid, no kept capabilities, verified
  that setuid(0) fails. adb shell/push/pull therefore run as that user.
* The authorization ("framework") socket is /run/adbd/adbd, mode 0600,
  owned by $ADBD_USER, for the on-phone confirmation prompt.
* USB FunctionFS only: no TCP fallback listener on port 5555 and no
  service.adb.tcp.port / persist.adb.tcp.port handling.
* umask 022 instead of 000 for adbd and the shells it spawns; HOME,
  USER, LOGNAME and SHELL of $ADBD_USER for the shells.
* adb push keeps the host file mode minus group/other write (Android
  widened the user bits to group/other).

